<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<% end %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">Connect <%= @device.name %></h1>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-800 bg-amber-950/30 p-5 text-amber-200">
    <p>This private connection address is shown once. Anyone with it can download books selected for this reader<%= " and relay this reader's Store requests" if @device.store_coexistence? %>. Keep it secret.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-800 bg-gray-900 p-5 text-sm text-gray-300" data-testid="kobo-mode">
    <% if @device.store_coexistence? %>
      <p class="font-semibold text-white">Mode: Kobo Store + Shelfarr</p>
      <p class="mt-2">Keep the reader signed in to its Kobo account. Your Store library, purchases and Store reading places keep syncing, and Shelfarr books arrive beside them. Shelfarr passes Store requests to Kobo using the reader's own sign-in and does not save it.</p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="font-semibold text-white">Mode: Shelfarr books only</p>
      <p class="mt-2">Store syncing pauses while this address is in use. Store books already on the reader stay. Restore the original endpoint to sync new purchases again.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-300">
    <li>Connect this Kobo to your computer by USB. Back up <code class="text-gray-200">.kobo/Kobo/Kobo eReader.conf</code> from the reader, including its original <code>api_endpoint</code>.</li>
    <li>Open the configuration file with a plain text editor. In the existing <code>[OneStoreServices]</code> section, replace only the <code>api_endpoint</code> line with:</li>
  </ol>
  <pre class="overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap break-all rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-900 p-4 text-sm text-green-300" data-testid="kobo-endpoint">api_endpoint=<%= @endpoint %></pre>
  <ol start="3" class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-300">
    <li>Save the file, safely eject the Kobo, then restart it. Open a library ebook in Shelfarr and choose <strong>Send to Kobo</strong>.</li>
    <li>On the Kobo, connect to Wi-Fi and tap <strong>Sync</strong>. Books arrive when the reader syncs; Shelfarr cannot wake it remotely.</li>
  </ol>
  <section class="rounded-lg border border-gray-800 bg-gray-900 p-5 text-sm text-gray-300" aria-labelledby="kobo-restore-heading">
    <h2 id="kobo-restore-heading" class="font-semibold text-white">To go back to Kobo only</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">Put your saved line back. If the backup is lost, the stock line is:</p>
    <pre class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap break-all rounded border border-gray-700 bg-gray-950 p-3 text-gray-200" data-testid="kobo-store-endpoint">api_endpoint=<%= KoboDevice::STORE_ENDPOINT %></pre>
    <p class="mt-2 text-gray-400">Do not sign out of, reset or delete the database on the reader to troubleshoot this connection; that can remove downloaded books.</p>
  </section>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Use a different connection for each physical reader. If the connection address is lost, regenerate it from the reader's settings. You can change the mode there later without editing the reader again.</p>
  <%= link_to "Done · manage reader", kobo_device_path(@device), class: "inline-block rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white hover:bg-blue-500" %>
</div>
